From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libc: guest system, popen and posix_spawn launch as bionic's

apklayer patch (docs/PATCHES.md). system and popen resolved to glibc's: the
host /bin/sh with the host environment. posix_spawn[p] and their attribute and
file-action calls resolved to glibc's too, whose posix_spawnattr_t (336 bytes)
and posix_spawn_file_actions_t (80 bytes) overran bionic's pointer-sized
objects, and posix_spawnp searched the host PATH. AOSP spawn.cpp's records and
accessors are kept and converted to glibc's at launch (file-action paths
through the path layer, POSIX_SPAWN_CLOEXEC_DEFAULT as closes after the
actions); system.cpp and stdio.cpp popen/fclose run /system/bin/sh with the
guest environment through the preload's guest spawn (path mapping, scripts,
Android programs through btload). posix_spawnp searches the parent's guest
PATH. As bionic, only a failed fork is an error: a later failure is a child
that exits with 127. popen children are tracked beside the glibc FILE, so
fclose and pclose (one function in bionic) both wait for them. bionic_execve
takes the guest exec entry.

